                                                 Business Question 3 
Which merchants have the highest number of fraudulent transactions, highest fraud rates, and highest fraudulent transaction values


                                     Query
SELECT
    merchant,

    SUM(CASE
        WHEN fraud = 1 THEN 1
        ELSE 0
    END) AS fraudulent_transactions,

    ROUND(
        SUM(CASE
            WHEN fraud = 1 THEN 1
            ELSE 0
        END) * 100.0/ COUNT(*),
        2
    ) AS fraud_rate,
    ROUND(
        SUM(CASE
            WHEN fraud = 1 THEN amount
            ELSE 0
        END),2) AS fraudulent_transaction_value
FROM fraud_detection_data
GROUP BY merchant
ORDER BY fraud_rate DESC;

                                                                              INSIGHT:
The analysis shows that fraud risk is concentrated differently across merchants. M1294758098 had the highest fraud rate at 96.34%, M732195782 had the highest fraudulent transaction 
value at approximately $1.35M, while M480139044 had the highest number of fraudulent transactions with 1,634 cases. This suggests that different merchants may represent different types 
of fraud risk and should be investigated using both fraud rate and fraud volume/value

                                                                            
                                                                             Recommendation
Prioritize high-risk merchants for further investigation and strengthen transaction screening around merchants with unusually high fraud rates or fraudulent transaction values.
Additional authentication and fraud-prevention controls can be considered for high-risk transactions and merchant activity.
